{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>From the storm</b> — like his companions. The meaning is that HaShem answered Job regarding his words, to rebuke him and to make him know that he does not know the ways of HaShem, which are general, even though the particular. And when HaShem finished rebuking him, Job was silent; HaShem answered and said to him: Why will you not answer?! And he replied with an unfitting word and said: I will not answer. Then HaShem said to him: Since you will not acknowledge the truth and think in your heart that you are wise, I will ask you; make it known to me. And this — that you were silent, do you thereby consent to overturn the laws of wisdom that I have established in the world? Will you condemn me, that you may be in the right?!"], :book :job, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 40, :notes {0 "Reading כאשר השלים as 'when HaShem finished'; the clause אף כי הפרט ('even though the particular') is elliptical, likely meaning 'even the particular,' but rendered hyper-literally without expansion."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Job -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/eyov/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:05:23.801621434Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}